WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:19.646
December 31 Dear Daddy Longlegs, I meant to thank you for your Christmas check before today.

2
00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.690
But life in the McBride house is very busy!

3
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.812
I used the money for a new evening gown.

4
00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:31.136
I must confess that I didn't need a new gown.

5
00:00:32.424 --> 00:00:33.325
I just wanted one!

6
00:00:34.585 --> 00:00:36.887
I've been having the most wonderful vacation.

7
00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:42.670
Sallie lives in a big, old-fashioned brick house.

8
00:00:45.031 --> 00:00:48.193
It's the kind of house I used to imagine when I lived at the orphanage.

9
00:00:49.294 --> 00:00:52.015
I never imagined that I'd step inside such a place.

10
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:54.617
But here I am!

11
00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:59.500
I think Sallie is surprised at how much I like her house.

12
00:01:03.132 --> 00:01:06.835
On our first day here, she showed me around, and I couldn't stop talking.

13
00:01:06.855 --> 00:01:09.577
"There are so many rooms!"

14
00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:10.238
I said.

15
00:01:10.258 --> 00:01:12.580
"I'll probably get lost."

16
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.543
"We did lose my little brother, Tom, one rainy day.

17
00:01:18.625 --> 00:01:20.927
We were playing hide-and-seek and couldn't find him.

18
00:01:22.888 --> 00:01:25.090
We finally gave up and went downstairs.

19
00:01:26.111 --> 00:01:30.014
Half an hour later, he came sliding down the banister in the front hall!"

20
00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.633
"You have so many fireplaces!"

21
00:01:35.954 --> 00:01:37.995
I said as we stepped into one of the parlors.

22
00:01:39.335 --> 00:01:40.156
Sallie laughed.

23
00:01:41.136 --> 00:01:45.119
"We'll make popcorn over the fire one night.

24
00:01:46.599 --> 00:01:48.741
Speaking of food, let's go visit the kitchen.

25
00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:51.542
We should say hello to Mrs.

26
00:01:51.622 --> 00:01:52.703
Jamison, the cook."

27
00:01:54.624 --> 00:01:57.625
We stepped into a great big sunny kitchen.

28
00:01:59.306 --> 00:02:03.693
Mrs. Jamison, a large, cheerful woman, was busy making pies.

29
00:02:05.174 --> 00:02:06.835
She stopped to give Sallie a hug.

30
00:02:06.855 --> 00:02:10.677
"I saved you a piece of dough to bake."

31
00:02:11.838 --> 00:02:13.919
The cook pointed to a miniature pie plate.

32
00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.523
sprinkle it with cinnamon sugar," Sallie said to me.

33
00:02:21.543 --> 00:02:23.924
"That'll make it taste even better."

34
00:02:27.526 --> 00:02:32.193
Sallie put the dough in the oven, and in a few minutes, we were eating a wonderful treat!

35
00:02:34.674 --> 00:02:38.596
All the meals here are delicious, and we have such fun at the table.

36
00:02:40.356 --> 00:02:43.338
Everybody laughs and jokes and talks at once.

37
00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.741
Besides Sallie's parents, her grandmother and siblings live here.

38
00:02:52.922 --> 00:02:57.164
Sallie's sister, Ellen, is only three, and she's the sweetest little thing.

39
00:02:58.812 --> 00:03:03.174
Sallie's younger brother, Tom, is always getting scolded, but in a loving way.

40
00:03:05.155 --> 00:03:07.916
He never remembers to wipe his feet when he enters the house.

41
00:03:10.177 --> 00:03:11.738
He reminds me of Master Jervie!

42
00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:17.840
Sallie also has a handsome big brother named Jimmy.

43
00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:22.222
He's a year older than we are, and he's a junior at Princeton.

44
00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.024
We've done so many things since I arrived.

45
00:03:26.984 --> 00:03:29.085
I can't even begin to tell you about them all.

46
00:03:30.646 --> 00:03:32.127
Mr. McBride owns a factory.

47
00:03:33.208 --> 00:03:36.790
On Christmas Eve he had a Christmas party for his employees' children.

48
00:03:39.511 --> 00:03:44.634
There was a Christmas tree, and one of the rooms in the factory was decorated with evergreens and

49
00:03:44.714 --> 00:03:48.336
holly. Jimmy was dressed as Santa Claus.

50
00:03:49.377 --> 00:03:51.298
He wore a white beard and a red suit.

51
00:03:52.679 --> 00:03:54.920
A pillow at his waist made him jolly and plump.

52
00:03:56.768 --> 00:04:00.151
"You're looking rather fat, brother dear," Sallie said.

53
00:04:00.171 --> 00:04:02.733
"Shh!" I poked her arm.

54
00:04:02.753 --> 00:04:05.115
"Don't let the children hear you.

55
00:04:06.116 --> 00:04:08.077
Let them think he's the real Santa Claus!"

56
00:04:08.097 --> 00:04:12.901
"This young lady is perfectly correct," Jimmy said to Sallie.

57
00:04:12.921 --> 00:04:16.004
"I don't know who you're calling brother dear."

58
00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:17.845
Then he turned to me.

59
00:04:17.865 --> 00:04:20.447
"I hope you've been a good girl this year.

60
00:04:21.508 --> 00:04:22.509
What would you like for Christmas?"

61
00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.611
I laughed.

62
00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:28.740
He's so much fun.

63
00:04:30.161 --> 00:04:32.201
Sallie and I helped him hand out the presents.

64
00:04:33.322 --> 00:04:36.122
It was a strange sensation to be handing out gifts.

65
00:04:37.323 --> 00:04:40.004
The whole scene reminded me of Christmas at the orphanage.

66
00:04:41.464 --> 00:04:45.945
Only this time I was playing the part of a kindly trustee instead of an orphan.

67
00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.306
I even kissed one sticky little boy.

68
00:04:50.547 --> 00:04:52.287
But I didn't pat anyone on the head.

69
00:04:53.427 --> 00:04:55.328
I used to hate being patted on the head!

70
00:04:57.216 --> 00:05:01.198
Right after Christmas the McBrides had a dance at their house—for me!

71
00:05:01.218 --> 00:05:08.361
"This is the first real ball I've ever attended," I said nervously to Sallie.

72
00:05:09.661 --> 00:05:10.942
She was helping me get dressed.

73
00:05:10.962 --> 00:05:14.983
"Well, you look beautiful!"

74
00:05:15.324 --> 00:05:15.764
she said.

75
00:05:15.784 --> 00:05:18.665
"Turn around so I can see the back of your dress."

76
00:05:20.266 --> 00:05:22.266
I was wearing my new evening gown.

77
00:05:22.286 --> 00:05:24.327
(Your Christmas present.

78
00:05:24.807 --> 00:05:25.788
Many thanks for that!)

79
00:05:26.884 --> 00:05:30.227
Plus white satin slippers and long white gloves.

80
00:05:31.808 --> 00:05:33.389
Sallie had to button the gloves for me.

81
00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.091
It's hard to do that by yourself.

82
00:05:36.111 --> 00:05:39.894
"You look perfect," Sallie said.

83
00:05:39.914 --> 00:05:42.295
"Jimmy will be very impressed."

84
00:05:44.097 --> 00:05:45.478
And indeed he was.

85
00:05:45.498 --> 00:05:48.900
"You look lovely," he said to me.

86
00:05:51.562 --> 00:05:53.624
And then we danced every dance.

87
00:05:58.744 --> 00:06:02.826
That is, until his mother said he must be polite and ask someone else.

88
00:06:04.687 --> 00:06:09.029
I was utterly, totally, completely happy that night.

89
00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.011
I only wished that Mrs.

90
00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.652
Lippett could have seen me dancing with Jimmy McBride.

91
00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:19.694
Please tell her about it the next time you visit the John Grier Home.

92
00:06:21.215 --> 00:06:24.689
Happy New Year, Judy P.S.

93
00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.994
Would you be disappointed if I didn't turn out to be a great author?

94
00:06:30.096 --> 00:06:35.082
What if I'm just a regular girl who likes wearing pretty clothes and dancing with good-looking boys?
